1
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:38,800
The placid banks of the Ipiranga heard the resounding cry of a heroic folk

2
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:47,500
And the sun of Liberty in shining beams shone in the homeland's sky at that instant.

3
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:55,000
If the pledge of this equality, we managed to conquer with strong arm,

4
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:03,000
In thy bosom, O Freedom, our chest defieth death itself!

5
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,000
O beloved, idolized homeland, hail, hail!

6
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:15,000
Brazil, an intense dream, a vivid ray of love and hope descends to earth

7
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:24,000
If in thy comely, smiling and limpid sky, the image of the Cross blazes.

8
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:32,000
Giant by thine own nature, thou art beautiful, thou art strong, an impavid colossus,

9
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:36,500
And thy future mirrors that greatness.

10
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,500
Adored Land

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,500
Amongst a thousand others art thou, Brazil,  O beloved homeland!

12
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Of the sons of this ground thou art kind mother,

13
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,500
Beloved homeland, Brazil!

14
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:57,500
Eternally lying on a splendid cradle, to the sound of the sea and under deep sky light

15
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:05,500
Thou flarest, O Brazil, crocket of America, illuminated by the sun of New World!

16
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:14,500
Than the showiest land, thy smiling, pretty prairies have more flowers

17
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:22,500
Our groves have more life, our life in thy bosom more loves

18
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:27,500
O beloved, idolized homeland, hail, hail!

19
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:35,500
Brazil, of eternal love be a symbol, the starred labarum which thou displayst

20
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:43,500
And say the laurel-green of thy pennant: 'Peace in the future and glory in the past.'

21
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:52,500
But if thou raisest the strong cudgel of Justice, thou wilt see that a son of thine flees not from battle,

22
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,500
Nor do those who love thee fear their own death.

23
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,500
Beloved Land,

24
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,500
Amongst a thousand others, art thou, Brazil, O beloved homeland!

25
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,500
Of the sons of this ground thou art gentle mother,

26
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,500
Beloved homeland, Brazil!